hing is on the complete graph of the odd","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order (pairs i < j lexicographic), and the circuit’s multigraph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lists the tree edges by position, then the matched pairs in that order. At most 3\/2 × the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shortest tour when the weights satisfy the triangle inequality (not checked).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/christofidesTour(weight:)-6qvc8","title":"christofidesTour(weight:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"christofidesTour"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","text":"Cycle"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/Graph/isEulerian":{"url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/iseulerian","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isEulerian","abstract":[{"text":"Whether some closed trail uses every edge exactly once: every degree is even (a self-loop","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counts 2) and the vertices with edges are connected. Isolated vertices are ignored","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(igraph’s and JGraphT’s rule; NetworkX counts them), and an edgeless graph, the empty","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"graph included, is Eulerian (igraph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"igraph_is_eulerian"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"has_cycle"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"isEulerian","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isEulerian"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/Graph/hamiltonianPath(from:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"The first Hamiltonian path from ","type":"text"},{"code":"start","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in the same search order.","type":"text"}],"title":"hamiltonianPath(from:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/hamiltonianPath(from:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/hamiltonianpath(from:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"hamiltonianPath"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4PathV","